     originally published.
  d. "Work Based on the Software" means any modification, translation,
     adaptation, or extension of the Software, and any work that incorporates the
     Software or a substantial portion of it.
  e. "User" or "you" means any person or organization that uses, operates,
     modifies, hosts, or distributes the Software.
  f. "Eligible User" means a User that meets the requirements of Section 2.
  g. "Full-Time Equivalent Worker" means one full-time position under the
     customary full-time working hours of the User's jurisdiction. Part-time
     positions are added up proportionally. Employees, working owners, and
     individual contractors working for the enterprise are counted. The number is
     the average over the Fiscal Year concerned.
  h. "Fiscal Year" means the twelve-month accounting period of the User. If the
     User has not yet completed a Fiscal Year, revenue and workers are measured
     from the time the User began operating, and revenue is annualized.
  i. "Installation Information" means any methods, procedures, authorization
     keys, or other information required to install and run modified versions of
     the Software on a device.
  j. "Reference Bodies" has the meaning given in Section 3(b).

1. ATTRIBUTION
The above copyright notice, this permission notice, and a clear attribution
to the original author(s) must be included in all copies or substantial
portions of the Software.

2. ELIGIBLE USERS
The User of the Software must be one of the following:
  a. An individual person, laboring for themselves and not for, on behalf of,
     or at the direction of any other person or organization (whether as
     employee, contractor, freelancer, or otherwise).
  b. A non-profit organization.
  c. An educational institution.
  d. An organization that seeks shared profit for all of its members, and
     allows non-members to set the cost of their labor.
  e. A small commercial enterprise that employs fewer than five (5) Full-Time
     Equivalent Workers AND generates less than $100,000 USD in gross annual
     revenue in the preceding Fiscal Year.

For the purpose of subsection 2(e), the revenue and employee count shall be
calculated cumulatively to include the entity, its parent companies, subsidiaries,
affiliates, and any corporate group it belongs to. Revenue in a currency other
than U.S. dollars is converted at the average official exchange rate for the
Fiscal Year concerned, as published by a recognized central bank. If the User is
an organization with owners operating under section 2(d), then all owners must be
workers and all workers must be owners with equal equity and/or equal vote.

If a User that is eligible solely under 2(e) ceases to meet either condition of
2(e), it remains an Eligible User for three (3) months after the date on which it
ceased to meet that condition (the "Transition Period"). Before the Transition
Period ends, it must stop all use of the Software or obtain a separate written
license from the Copyright Holder.

3. RESTRICTED USERS & USES
Notwithstanding Section 2 and any other provision of this License, the Software
MUST NOT be used, operated, modified, or distributed by:
  a. Law enforcement agencies, military entities, intelligence agencies, private
     security contractors working under their authority, or any entity working for,
     contracting with, or operating under the control or direction of any of them.
  b. Any person or entity that a Reference Body has found, in a published
     judgment, decision, report, or finding, to be involved in violations of
     international human rights as set out in the United Nations Universal
     Declaration of Human Rights, in systematic labor exploitation, in forced
     labor, or in severe environmental destruction.

"Reference Bodies" are the institutions listed in the file REFERENCE-LIST.md as
published with ECPL v1.3 at
https://github.com/FreakySneaky787/Ethical-Copyleft-Public-License/blob/v1.3/REFERENCE-LIST.md
That list forms part of this License and changes only with a new version of the
ECPL. A restriction under 3(b) applies from the date the finding is published. It
ends from the date on which the finding is withdrawn by the Reference Body or set
aside by a competent court. This Section 3 prevails over Section 2, including
the Transition Period.

4. COPYLEFT REQUIREMENT (SOURCE DISTRIBUTION)
If you modify, transform, extend, or build upon the Software, or integrate
it into another project, you may distribute or make available the resulting
Work Based on the Software ONLY under the exact terms of this License. You must
make the full source code of your modifications freely available to all
Eligible Users under these same conditions.

Each recipient to whom you convey the Software or a Work Based on the Software
receives a license directly from the Copyright Holder and every Contributor
on the terms of this License. That license does not derive from you. You are not
responsible for enforcing compliance by third parties.

5. NETWORK COPYLEFT, SERVICE PROVISION & INTERACTION BOUNDARIES
If you run the Software or a Work Based on the Software on a server or isolated
environment (including containers, virtual machines, microservices, or cloud
infrastructure) and permit other users or software components to interact
with it remotely over a network or application programming interface (API),
you MUST offer those network users access to the corresponding complete source
code of your version under the terms of this License, at no extra charge.

This Section applies to the Software and Works Based on the Software only. For
the avoidance of doubt, a separate and independent program that merely
communicates with the Software via an API, RPC, shared memory, or network
protocol is not, by that fact alone, a Work Based on the Software.

6. SUSPENSION, CURE & TERMINATION
a. Any use, copying, modification, or distribution of the Software not in strict
   compliance with the terms and conditions of this License automatically
   suspends your rights under this License with immediate effect. While your
   rights are suspended, you must not use, host, or distribute the Software,
   except as necessary to restore compliance.
b. If you restore full compliance within thirty (30) days after the earlier of
   (i) written notice of the violation from the Copyright Holder or a
   Contributor and (ii) the date on which you knew or reasonably should have
   known of the violation, your rights are reinstated as of the date compliance
   is restored. Reinstatement does not release you from liability for
   non-compliant conduct before that date.
c. If you do not restore compliance within that period, your rights terminate
   permanently. You must then immediately cease all use, hosting, and
   distribution of the Software and destroy all copies in your possession or
   control.
d. Suspension or termination of your rights does not affect the licenses that
   recipients hold under Section 4.

